  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p><b>Use Kinesis Data Firehose to deliver streaming data directly into Amazon Redshift for analysis</b> is the best option in this scenario. Kinesis Data Firehose efficiently ingests high-velocity streaming data and loads it directly into Amazon Redshift, a fully managed, petabyte-scale data warehouse service designed for analytics using standard SQL. This approach allows your business intelligence team to continue using SQL for complex queries across large datasets as soon as new data is available.</p><p>Why are the other options less suitable?</p><ul><li><i>Leverage EMR clusters with Apache Spark.</i> and <i>Utilize EMR clusters running Hive.</i> provide great scalability and flexibility for big data processing, but they require expertise in Spark or Hive, extra infrastructure management, and are not optimal for teams that primarily rely on SQL-based workflows and need near real-time streaming analytics.</li><li><i>Apply Kinesis Data Firehose streaming directly into Amazon RDS databases.</i> is impractical for petabyte-scale, high-velocity workloads since RDS is intended for transactional databases and cannot efficiently scale for massive analytics queries; additionally, RDS is not built for columnar storage or data warehousing.</li></ul><p><b>Tips:</b> For analysis of massive, fast-arriving, well-structured datasets with SQL, Redshift offers the ideal mix of performance, scalability, and support for standard BI tools, especially when paired with Kinesis Firehose for streaming ingestion.</p>",
